-- What an author writes today to refuse the request while a listing points at
-- the seller: the same `never`, and the listing's seller weakened to
-- `? initially required` so that check V24 passes. The `never` means no
-- listing's seller can ever go absent, yet the field is declared as one that
-- may, so every rule that reads `listing.seller` must answer for an absence
-- that cannot happen.

act Seller {
    name: text
}

act Listing {
    title: text
    seller: one Seller? initially required
}

transient act CloseAccount {
    seller: one Seller
}

never (CloseAccount where exists (Listing where seller == this.seller))

rule ApplyClose when CloseAccount {
    delete seller
}
